  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint IOM-WHO Organization and Delivery of the 2024 PSEA Coordinator Course</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, funded by the World Health Organization (WHO), is supporting costs of organizing and delivering the 2024 Protection from Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (PSEA) Coordinator global training course. The PSEA Coordinator Training is a four-day training aiming to equip PSEA Coordinators and potential PSEA Coordinators to effectively support PSEA activities at country level following good practice and defined roles and responsibilities in line with the Generic PSEA Coordinator TORs. To strengthen coherence between the course alumni talent pool and future deployments of Coordinators, the Training merged into the new PSEACap Roster talent management (absorbing and expanding on existing PSEA Coordinator rosters). In 2024, the next delivery of the course is delivered face-to-face jointly by the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and WHO. The contribution from WHO to IOM supports professional updates and improvements to the course content and brings the delivery live after four years of online methodology. IOM continues to handle the logistical course organization, and IOM and WHO together ensure the usual good collaboration with the IASC Protection from Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment Technical Advisory Group and United Nations Office of the Special Coordinator on Sexual Exploitation and Abuse on preparing and facilitating the annual course.</narrative>
  </description>
